Subject: Bind the textures of a batch in one go (glbatchtmu)

The world batches selected a texture unit for each bind (glActiveTexture, glBindTexture) and went back to unit 0 after the textures of a slot and after the lightmaps, so a batch that changed its lightmap, its normal-map lightmap and the textures of its slot made up to 8 glActiveTexture calls, most of them to the unit that was active already or to one that was selected again a call later (288 a frame on cave).

With glbatchtmu 1 (the default) changeslottmus and changebatchtmus only note the binds that changed, and renderbatch issues them right before the draw of the batch: the unit that is active first, then the others in order, one glActiveTexture for each unit that changes. renderbatches returns to unit 0 once, at its end. GL's state at every draw is the same. 0 is the old code.

